<div id="show-message-upgrade-complete" class="hidden show-message">
    <div class="box">
        <div class="box-inner">
            <h2>Warning</h2>

            <p>
                This is the final version of Sprucemarks.
            </p>

            <p>
                On November 1, 2026 this software will be removed from GitHub, Google, Microsoft, Mozilla, and other software distribution locations.
            </p>

            <p>
                If you wish to keep using Sprucemarks or any of my other software going forward, you must download your own copy from <a href="https://github.com/nightmode?tab=repositories&sort=name" rel="noopener noreferrer" target="_blank">GitHub</a>. Each available project will have a releases section with an archive version you can download. All projects are in the public domain so you can modify, remix, redistribute, or do whatever you want.
            </p>

            <p>
                You can run local extensions by activating developer mode in your browser and loading the extracted files from a location on your hard drive. It is a bit more intial setup but then you are in control.
            </p>

            <p>
                If you DO NOT download Sprucemarks, you will likely lose access to it once it disappears on November 1, 2026.
            </p>

            <p>
                I know ownership is a chore but only ownership can ensure you enjoy your favorite movies, tv shows, music, books, and software as you travel through time. Take care.
            </p>
        </div><!-- box-inner -->
    </div><!-- box -->
</div><!-- show-message-upgrade-complete -->

<div id="show-message-chrome-extensions-toolbar" class="hidden show-message">
    <div class="box">
        <div class="box-inner">
            <p>
                Google Chrome hides extensions by default but you can use the extensions <span class="no-wrap">menu <img src="/images/messages/chrome/puzzle.png?version=2022.7.2.0" width="18" height="18" class="icon icon-chrome-puzzle" alt></span> in the upper right of Chrome to enable the <span class="no-wrap">pin <img src="/images/messages/chrome/pin.png?version=2022.7.2.0" width="18" height="18" class="icon icon-chrome-pin" alt></span> option for Sprucemarks.
            </p>

            <p>
                The above procedure will allow the Sprucemarks <span class="no-wrap">icon <img src="/images/messages/chrome/tree.png?version=2022.7.2.0" width="18" height="18" class="icon" alt></span> to be visible and enable one-click access.
            </p>

            <p>
                <input class="button show-message-dismiss" data-id="show-message-chrome-extensions-toolbar" type="button" value="Continue">
            </p>
        </div><!-- box-inner -->
    </div><!-- box -->
</div><!-- show-message-chrome-extensions-toolbar -->

<div id="show-message-edge-extensions-toolbar" class="hidden show-message">
    <div class="box">
        <div class="box-inner">
            <p>
                Microsoft Edge hides extensions by default but you can use the extensions <span class="no-wrap">menu <img src="/images/messages/edge/puzzle.png?version=2022.7.2.0" width="18" height="18" class="icon icon-edge-puzzle" alt></span> in the upper right of Edge to enable the <span class="no-wrap">eye <img src="/images/messages/edge/eye.png?version=2022.7.2.0" width="18" height="18" class="icon icon-edge-eye" alt></span> option for Sprucemarks.
            </p>

            <p>
                The above procedure will allow the Sprucemarks <span class="no-wrap">icon <img src="/images/messages/edge/tree.png?version=2022.7.2.0" width="18" height="18" class="icon" alt></span> to be visible and enable one-click access.
            </p>

            <p>
                <input class="button show-message-dismiss" data-id="show-message-edge-extensions-toolbar" type="button" value="Continue">
            </p>
        </div><!-- box-inner -->
    </div><!-- box -->
</div><!-- show-message-edge-extensions-toolbar -->

<div id="show-message-firefox-extensions-toolbar" class="hidden show-message">
    <div class="box">
        <div class="box-inner">
            <p>
                Mozilla Firefox hides extensions by default but you can use the extensions <span class="no-wrap">menu <img src="/images/messages/firefox/puzzle.png?version=2025.6.26.0" width="18" height="18" class="icon" alt></span> in the upper right of Firefox to click on the <span class="no-wrap">gear <img src="/images/messages/firefox/gear.png?version=2025.6.26.0" width="18" height="18" class="icon" alt></span> for Sprucemarks which will then reveal a "Pin to Toolbar" option.
            </p>

            <p>
                The above procedure will allow the Sprucemarks <span class="no-wrap">icon <img src="/images/messages/firefox/tree.png?version=2025.6.26.0" width="18" height="18" class="icon" alt></span> to be visible and enable one-click access.
            </p>

            <p>
                <input class="button show-message-dismiss" data-id="show-message-firefox-extensions-toolbar" type="button" value="Continue">
            </p>
        </div><!-- box-inner -->
    </div><!-- box -->
</div><!-- show-message-firefox-extensions-toolbar -->